# tests/litscan/spanarms.rxt -- span arms unit E1 ([REQ-EMPTYCAT]'s quantified
# half; docs/design/span_arms.md §4, T2 row 1 in §6): A REPEAT OF A WIDTH-0 BODY
# IS CAT'S UNIT. The necessary run joins the bytes on its two sides
# (src/facts/req.c `rb_rep_rows`), so `abcd(?:\b)*efgh` states `abcdefgh`
# where it stated `efgh`. Every expectation is libpcre2-8 10.46's
# (tests/lib/p2probe.c, lane sae1, 2026-11-09), never pcrec's. Each block
# runs on the default route and again under `engine vm`: the run pre-check
# is emitted into both engines' search entries. W-R4 and S-g are the unit's
# two sabotage witnesses (rows S1906, S1905); a sabotaged run is absent from
# the subject, clears the 16-bit floor, and is pinned by no k-set walk, so
# the pre-check answers NOMATCH where libpcre2 matches.

# W-R4 (span_arms §3.6): T2 row 1 tests the body's MAXIMUM width; `(?:c?){2}` is not width 0, so the run stays `de` (or `ab`); S1906 reads the minimum width, claims `abde` and deletes every match that takes a `c`
pattern ab(?:c?){2}de
features all
m "abcde" 0 5
m "abde" 0 4
m "abccde" 0 6
n "abcccde"
m "xxabcdexx" 2 7
n "abce"

# W-R4 (span_arms §3.6): T2 row 1 tests the body's MAXIMUM width; `(?:c?){2}` is not width 0, so the run stays `de` (or `ab`); S1906 reads the minimum width, claims `abde` and deletes every match that takes a `c` [engine vm]
pattern ab(?:c?){2}de
features all
engine vm
m "abcde" 0 5
m "abde" 0 4
m "abccde" 0 6
n "abcccde"
m "xxabcdexx" 2 7
n "abce"

# S-g (alt_normal_form §9 S2, spelled for E1's site): a backreference CONSUMES; `\1*` is not width 0, so the run is `abx`; S1905 tests "carries no run" instead of width 0, sends the backreference to row 1 and claims `abxy`
pattern (ab)x\1*y
features all
m "abxaby" 0 6
m "abxy" 0 4
m "abxababy" 0 8
n "abxa"
n "abxaay"

# S-g (alt_normal_form §9 S2, spelled for E1's site): a backreference CONSUMES; `\1*` is not width 0, so the run is `abx`; S1905 tests "carries no run" instead of width 0, sends the backreference to row 1 and claims `abxy` [engine vm]
pattern (ab)x\1*y
features all
engine vm
m "abxaby" 0 6
m "abxy" 0 4
m "abxababy" 0 8
n "abxa"
n "abxaay"

# E-2: a min-0 repeat of an empty group is the unit; the run joins across it (`abcdefgh`)
pattern abcd(?:)*efgh
features all
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"
m "xxabcdefghxx" 2 10

# E-2: a min-0 repeat of an empty group is the unit; the run joins across it (`abcdefgh`) [engine vm]
pattern abcd(?:)*efgh
features all
engine vm
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"
m "xxabcdefghxx" 2 10

# E-3: a min-0 repeat of a width-0 assertion (the anchor wrapper's `<anchor EMPTY>` under `*`) is the unit
pattern abcd(?:\b)*efgh
features all
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"
m "xxabcdefghxx" 2 10

# E-3: a min-0 repeat of a width-0 assertion (the anchor wrapper's `<anchor EMPTY>` under `*`) is the unit [engine vm]
pattern abcd(?:\b)*efgh
features all
engine vm
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"
m "xxabcdefghxx" 2 10

# T2 row 1 at m >= 1: the copies of a width-0 body coincide; this pattern never matches (no boundary between `d` and `e`), and every run is sound for it
pattern abcd(?:\b)+efgh
features all
n "abcdefgh"
n "abcd"
n "efgh"

# T2 row 1 at m >= 1: the copies of a width-0 body coincide; this pattern never matches (no boundary between `d` and `e`), and every run is sound for it [engine vm]
pattern abcd(?:\b)+efgh
features all
engine vm
n "abcdefgh"
n "abcd"
n "efgh"

# E-3: the anchor wrapper under `*` (`^` lowered to its context node)
pattern abcd(?:^)*efgh
features all
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcd"
m "xabcdefgh" 1 9

# E-3: the anchor wrapper under `*` (`^` lowered to its context node) [engine vm]
pattern abcd(?:^)*efgh
features all
engine vm
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcd"
m "xabcdefgh" 1 9

# E-3: the anchor wrapper under `?`
pattern abcd(?:$)?efgh
features all
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"

# E-3: the anchor wrapper under `?` [engine vm]
pattern abcd(?:$)?efgh
features all
engine vm
m "abcdefgh" 0 8
n "abcdxefgh"

# E-3: a min-0 repeat of a lookahead (its body not read: the run is `xyabzw` through the repeat, never into the body)
pattern xy(?:(?=a))*abzw
features all
m "xyabzw" 0 6
n "xyzw"
n "xyabab"

# E-3: a min-0 repeat of a lookahead (its body not read: the run is `xyabzw` through the repeat, never into the body) [engine vm]
pattern xy(?:(?=a))*abzw
features all
engine vm
m "xyabzw" 0 6
n "xyzw"
n "xyabab"

# T2 row 1 at m = n >= 1: three copies of `\B` are one zero-width stretch
pattern ab(?:\B){3}cd
features all
m "abcd" 0 4
m "xabcdx" 1 5
n "ab-cd"

# T2 row 1 at m = n >= 1: three copies of `\B` are one zero-width stretch [engine vm]
pattern ab(?:\B){3}cd
features all
engine vm
m "abcd" 0 4
m "xabcdx" 1 5
n "ab-cd"

# ---- span arms unit E2 (T3 E-1, E-4, E-5 as the plain unit; docs/design/span_arms.md §4.1): a node that
# consumes nothing is CAT's unit, so the run joins across `\b`, `\B`, `$`, `^`, `\G`, `\K`, `\A`, `\z`,
# lookarounds of either lowering and the empty string (src/facts/req.c `rb_zero_rows`). Expectations libpcre2-8 10.46's
# (tests/lib/p2probe.c, lane sae2, 2026-11-09). S-L, W-E3 and S-g here are rows S1925, S1926, S1927.

# S-L, spelled for E2's site (span_arms §4.1 S16, E-5 as the plain unit): a positive lookbehind consumes nothing, so the run is `xyzabc` across it; S1925 walks its body as CONSUMED, claims `xyzyzabc` and the pre-check deletes every match
pattern xyz(?<=yz)abc
features all
m "xyzabc" 0 6
n "xyzyzabc"
m "qqxyzabcq" 2 8
n "xyabc"

# S-L, spelled for E2's site (span_arms §4.1 S16, E-5 as the plain unit): a positive lookbehind consumes nothing, so the run is `xyzabc` across it; S1925 walks its body as CONSUMED, claims `xyzyzabc` and the pre-check deletes every match [engine vm]
pattern xyz(?<=yz)abc
features all
engine vm
m "xyzabc" 0 6
n "xyzyzabc"
m "qqxyzabcq" 2 8
n "xyabc"

# S-L (span_arms §5.7, E2's correct value): a lookbehind at the start leaves the run `bar`; S1925 walks its body as CONSUMED, claims `foobar` at offset 0 and a search from 3 finds no attempt
pattern (?<=foo)bar
features all
m "foobar" 3 6
ms 3 "foobar" 3 6
ns 4 "foobar"
n "fobar"

# S-L (span_arms §5.7, E2's correct value): a lookbehind at the start leaves the run `bar`; S1925 walks its body as CONSUMED, claims `foobar` at offset 0 and a search from 3 finds no attempt [engine vm]
pattern (?<=foo)bar
features all
engine vm
m "foobar" 3 6
ms 3 "foobar" 3 6
ns 4 "foobar"
n "fobar"

# W-E3 (span_arms §4.5, E-4): a negative lookbehind consumes nothing, so the run is `xycd` across it; S1926 walks its body as CONSUMED, claims `xyabcd` and deletes `xycd`
pattern xy(?<!ab)cd
features all
m "xycd" 0 4
n "xyabcd"
ns 2 "abcd"
m "abxycd" 2 6

# W-E3 (span_arms §4.5, E-4): a negative lookbehind consumes nothing, so the run is `xycd` across it; S1926 walks its body as CONSUMED, claims `xyabcd` and deletes `xycd` [engine vm]
pattern xy(?<!ab)cd
features all
engine vm
m "xycd" 0 4
n "xyabcd"
ns 2 "abcd"
m "abxycd" 2 6

# S-g (alt_normal_form §9 S2, at E2's site): a backreference is TEXT ANY, never T3's unit, so the run stays `abx`; S1927 sends TEXT ANY to T3, claims `abxy` and deletes `abxaby`
pattern (ab)x\1y
features all
m "abxaby" 0 6
g 1 0 2
n "abxy"
n "abxaay"

# S-g (alt_normal_form §9 S2, at E2's site): a backreference is TEXT ANY, never T3's unit, so the run stays `abx`; S1927 sends TEXT ANY to T3, claims `abxy` and deletes `abxaby` [engine vm]
pattern (ab)x\1y
features all
engine vm
m "abxaby" 0 6
g 1 0 2
n "abxy"
n "abxaay"

# E-4 `\b`: the run is `foo-bar` across the boundary
pattern foo\b-bar
features all
m "foo-bar" 0 7
m "xfoo-barx" 1 8
n "foo-baz"

# E-4 `\b`: the run is `foo-bar` across the boundary [engine vm]
pattern foo\b-bar
features all
engine vm
m "foo-bar" 0 7
m "xfoo-barx" 1 8
n "foo-baz"

# E-4 `\B`: the run is `abcd` across it
pattern ab\Bcd
features all
m "abcd" 0 4
m "xabcdx" 1 5
n "ab-cd"

# E-4 `\B`: the run is `abcd` across it [engine vm]
pattern ab\Bcd
features all
engine vm
m "abcd" 0 4
m "xabcdx" 1 5
n "ab-cd"

# E-4 `$` before the final newline: the run is `ab\n`
pattern ab$\n
features all
m "ab\n" 0 3
n "ab\nx"
m "xab\n" 1 4

# E-4 `$` before the final newline: the run is `ab\n` [engine vm]
pattern ab$\n
features all
engine vm
m "ab\n" 0 3
n "ab\nx"
m "xab\n" 1 4

# E-4 multiline `$` (an A_CTX): the run is `ab\ncd`
pattern (?m)ab$\ncd
features all
m "ab\ncd" 0 5
m "xab\ncdx" 1 6
n "ab\nxcd"

# E-4 multiline `$` (an A_CTX): the run is `ab\ncd` [engine vm]
pattern (?m)ab$\ncd
features all
engine vm
m "ab\ncd" 0 5
m "xab\ncdx" 1 6
n "ab\nxcd"

# E-4 multiline `^` (an A_CTX): the run is `ab\ncd`
pattern (?m)ab\n^cd
features all
m "ab\ncd" 0 5
m "zab\ncdz" 1 6
n "ab\n cd"

# E-4 multiline `^` (an A_CTX): the run is `ab\ncd` [engine vm]
pattern (?m)ab\n^cd
features all
engine vm
m "ab\ncd" 0 5
m "zab\ncdz" 1 6
n "ab\n cd"

# E-4 `\K`: the run is `abcd` across it (the attempt's span; the reported match starts after `\K`)
pattern ab\Kcd
features all
m "abcd" 2 4
m "xabcdx" 3 5
n "abxcd"

# E-4 `\K`: the run is `abcd` across it (the attempt's span; the reported match starts after `\K`) [engine vm]
pattern ab\Kcd
features all
engine vm
m "abcd" 2 4
m "xabcdx" 3 5
n "abxcd"

# E-4 `\G` mid-pattern (never matches, so every run is sound: `abcd`)
pattern ab\Gcd
features all
n "abcd"
ns 2 "abcd"

# E-4 `\G` mid-pattern (never matches, so every run is sound: `abcd`) [engine vm]
pattern ab\Gcd
features all
engine vm
n "abcd"
ns 2 "abcd"

# E-4 `\A` mid-pattern (never matches)
pattern ab\Acd
features all
n "abcd"

# E-4 `\A` mid-pattern (never matches) [engine vm]
pattern ab\Acd
features all
engine vm
n "abcd"

# E-4 `\z` mid-pattern (never matches)
pattern ab\zcd
features all
n "abcd"

# E-4 `\z` mid-pattern (never matches) [engine vm]
pattern ab\zcd
features all
engine vm
n "abcd"

# E-4 a negative lookahead (span_arms §4.4): the run is `xac`, the body unread
pattern x(?!ab)ac
features all
m "xac" 0 3
n "xab"
m "zxacz" 1 4

# E-4 a negative lookahead (span_arms §4.4): the run is `xac`, the body unread [engine vm]
pattern x(?!ab)ac
features all
engine vm
m "xac" 0 3
n "xab"
m "zxacz" 1 4

# E-5 a one-character lookahead (lowered to A_CTX NEXT): the run is `abcd`
pattern ab(?=c)cd
features all
m "abcd" 0 4
n "abce"
m "xabcdx" 1 5

# E-5 a one-character lookahead (lowered to A_CTX NEXT): the run is `abcd` [engine vm]
pattern ab(?=c)cd
features all
engine vm
m "abcd" 0 4
n "abce"
m "xabcdx" 1 5

# E-5 a one-character lookbehind (lowered to A_CTX PREV): the run is `abcd`
pattern ab(?<=b)cd
features all
m "abcd" 0 4
n "abce"
m "xabcdx" 1 5

# E-5 a one-character lookbehind (lowered to A_CTX PREV): the run is `abcd` [engine vm]
pattern ab(?<=b)cd
features all
engine vm
m "abcd" 0 4
n "abce"
m "xabcdx" 1 5

# E-4 a one-character negative lookahead (A_CTX NOT_NEXT): the run is `abcd`
pattern ab(?!x)cd
features all
m "abcd" 0 4
n "abxd"
m "xabcdx" 1 5

# E-4 a one-character negative lookahead (A_CTX NOT_NEXT): the run is `abcd` [engine vm]
pattern ab(?!x)cd
features all
engine vm
m "abcd" 0 4
n "abxd"
m "xabcdx" 1 5

# E-4 a one-character negative lookbehind (A_CTX NOT_PREV): the run is `abcd`
pattern ab(?<!x)cd
features all
m "abcd" 0 4
m "xabcdx" 1 5
n "abd"

# E-4 a one-character negative lookbehind (A_CTX NOT_PREV): the run is `abcd` [engine vm]
pattern ab(?<!x)cd
features all
engine vm
m "abcd" 0 4
m "xabcdx" 1 5
n "abd"

# E-5 a positive lookahead (A_LOOK): the run is `xyabzw`, the body unread
pattern xy(?=ab)abzw
features all
m "xyabzw" 0 6
n "xyabab"
m "qxyabzwq" 1 7

# E-5 a positive lookahead (A_LOOK): the run is `xyabzw`, the body unread [engine vm]
pattern xy(?=ab)abzw
features all
